TommyDS HISTORY
===============

4.0 2026/10
===========
 * BREAKING CHANGE: tommy_tree_insert() now inserts elements with duplicate
   keys and has a void return type. Code that used its return
   value to detect duplicates must call the new tommy_tree_insert_unique().
   Tree search and removal select the first equal element in tree order.
 * BREAKING CHANGE: Renamed tommy_array_insert() to
   tommy_array_insert_tail() and tommy_arrayblk_insert() to
   tommy_arrayblk_insert_tail(). Callers must use the new names.
 * BREAKING CHANGE: Reimplemented tommy_hash_u32(), tommy_hash_u64(),
   tommy_strhash_u32(), and added tommy_strhash_u64() using MurmurHash3
   (x86_32 and x64_64) for significantly faster hashing. This is a breaking
   change because the resulting hash values are different from previous
   versions. tommy_hash_u32() and tommy_hash_u64() now produce identical hash
   results to tommy_strhash_u32() and tommy_strhash_u64() for 0-terminated
   strings.
 * Added tommy_hashtable_bucket_count(), tommy_hashtable_clear(),
   tommy_hashtable_empty(), tommy_hashtable_insert_unique(),
   tommy_hashtable_rehash_existing() and tommy_hashtable_to_list().
   These query table state, empty it while retaining buckets, insert only
   absent keys, update an existing node's hash, and drain nodes to a list.
 * Added tommy_hashdyn_bucket_count(), tommy_hashdyn_clear(),
   tommy_hashdyn_empty(), tommy_hashdyn_insert_unique(),
   tommy_hashdyn_rehash_existing(), tommy_hashdyn_reserve(),
   tommy_hashdyn_shrink() and tommy_hashdyn_to_list().
   In addition to state queries, reuse, unique insertion, rehashing, and
   list transfer, these can reserve or shrink the bucket allocation.
 * Added tommy_hashlin_bucket_count(), tommy_hashlin_clear(),
   tommy_hashlin_empty(), tommy_hashlin_insert_unique(),
   tommy_hashlin_rehash_existing() and tommy_hashlin_to_list().
   These provide state queries, reuse, unique insertion, rehashing, and
   transfer to a list for the linear hash table.
 * Added tommy_list_insert_before(), tommy_list_insert_after(),
   tommy_list_remove_head(), tommy_list_remove_tail(), tommy_list_prev(),
   tommy_list_move_head(), tommy_list_move_tail(), tommy_list_reverse()
   and tommy_list_swap().
   These add relative insertion, removal at either end, backward iteration,
   and ways to reorder or exchange list contents.
 * Added tommy_list_split(), tommy_list_prepend(),
   tommy_list_splice_before(), tommy_list_splice_after() and
   tommy_list_merge().
   These transfer ranges or whole lists without copying objects, and merge
   two sorted lists while preserving the order of equal elements.
 * Added tommy_tree_head(), tommy_tree_tail(), tommy_tree_next(),
   tommy_tree_prev(), tommy_tree_parent(), tommy_tree_empty(),
   tommy_tree_remove_head() and tommy_tree_remove_tail().
   These navigate the tree and its key order, test for emptiness, and remove
   its smallest or greatest element.
 * Added tommy_tree_search_greater_equal(),
   tommy_tree_search_greater_equal_compare(),
   tommy_tree_search_less_equal(),
   tommy_tree_search_less_equal_compare(), tommy_tree_insert_unique(),
   tommy_tree_remove_compare(), tommy_tree_clear() and tommy_tree_to_list().
   These find inclusive key bounds, keep unique insertion available, remove
   using a custom comparison, clear for reuse, and drain nodes to a list in
   tree order.
 * Added tommy_array_reserve(), tommy_arrayof_reserve(),
   tommy_arrayblk_reserve() and tommy_arrayblkof_reserve().
   These preallocate capacity to accommodate elements without increasing the
   initialized size or invalidating existing references.
 * Added tommy_array_resize(), tommy_arrayof_resize(),
   tommy_arrayblk_resize(), tommy_arrayblkof_resize(), tommy_array_clear(),
   tommy_arrayof_clear(), tommy_arrayblk_clear() and tommy_arrayblkof_clear().
   These allow changing the initialized size bidirectionally with automatic
   zeroing of unused slots upon shrinking, and clearing while preserving
   allocated capacity for immediate reuse.
 * Added tommy_array_shrink(), tommy_arrayof_shrink(),
   tommy_arrayblk_shrink() and tommy_arrayblkof_shrink().
   These release unused allocated segments or blocks without moving existing
   elements or altering their addresses.
 * Added tommy_arrayof_insert_tail() and tommy_arrayblkof_insert_tail().
   These append a zeroed record and return its address for direct access.
 * Added tommy_array_tail(), tommy_arrayof_tail(), tommy_arrayblk_tail(),
   tommy_arrayblkof_tail(), tommy_array_remove_tail(),
   tommy_arrayof_remove_tail(), tommy_arrayblk_remove_tail() and
   tommy_arrayblkof_remove_tail(). These access or remove the last element.
 * Added tommy_array_empty(), tommy_arrayof_empty(),
   tommy_arrayblk_empty(), tommy_arrayblkof_empty(),
   tommy_array_capacity(), tommy_arrayof_capacity(),
   tommy_arrayblk_capacity(), tommy_arrayblkof_capacity(),
   tommy_array_swap(), tommy_arrayof_swap(), tommy_arrayblk_swap() and
   tommy_arrayblkof_swap(). These query state or exchange whole arrays
   without moving stored elements.
 * Added tommy_array_foreach(), tommy_array_foreach_arg(),
   tommy_arrayof_foreach(), tommy_arrayof_foreach_arg(),
   tommy_arrayblk_foreach(), tommy_arrayblk_foreach_arg(),
   tommy_arrayblkof_foreach() and tommy_arrayblkof_foreach_arg().
   These iterate across initialized elements in order, passing the element
   pointer or in-place record reference to callback functions.


3.0 2025/11
===========
 * Added support for 64-bit platforms and 64-bit integers. When building on
   a 64-bit platform you can store more than $2^{32}$ objects in the containers.
   This doesn't apply to tries that are able to store only 32-bit integers,
   but you can change this with the TOMMY_TRIE_BIT and TOMMY_TRIE_INPLACE_BIT
   definitions.
 * Fixed undefined behavior in hashing functions. It could cause issues
   with vector instructions.
 * Reorganized some structures to avoid padding.
 * Removed the tommy_count_t type that is now always replaced by tommy_size_t.
 * Renamed the "key" field of the tommy_node_t to "index" to be more generic
   on the possible use.
 * Added TOMMY_API to override linkage features of the interface. Useful for
   amalgamations [Nodir Temirkhodjaev].

2.2 2018/02
===========
 * Removed tommy_list_remove_head_not_empty() as not used and wrongly
   implemented [Daniel Roethlisberger].

2.1 2016/11
===========
 * Added a new hash function for strings: tommy_strhash_u32().
 * Added a new tree implementation. It's not intended to be fast but useful if
   you need elements in order.
 * Fixed some references to TOMMY_ARRAYBLKOF_SIZE, where instead
   TOMMY_ARRAYBLK_SIZE was incorrectly used [Rocco].

2.0 2014/12
===========
 * Fixed a Segmentation Fault bug in the trie_inplace container when inserting
   duplicate elements.
 * Faster array and hashlin implementations when accessing elements.
 * Added new hashtable functions to iterate over all the elements.
 * Added a new tommy_calloc() function used for allocating initialized memory.
   If you redefined tommy_malloc(), likely you have to redefine also tommy_calloc().
 * Reached 100% code coverage in the regression test.
 * Different source code organization.
 * Added benchmark comparison with Binary Search Tesseract by Gregorius van
   den Hoven.

1.8 2013/12
===========
 * Fixed build of tommy_arrayblk in C++.
 * Changed the default node size of tommy_trie to fit a cache line of 64 bytes.
 * Added benchmark comparison with STX BTree.

1.7 2013/12
===========
 * Extended tommy_hashlin_done() to work also if the hashtable is not empty.
 * Removed the empty tommy_trie_done() because the real deallocation is done
   by the allocator.

1.6 2013/11
===========
 * Added a new tommy_arrayblk and tommy_arrayblkof types to store elements
   in an array minimizing memory occupation.

1.5 2013/06
===========
 * Fixed inline declaration to allow building with clang.
 * Added a new tommy_arrayof type to store in an array elements of arbitrary
   size.

1.4 2013/03
===========
 * Added benchmark comparison with Google BTree, and C++ map and unordered_map.
 * Benchmark for Linux is now compiled with "-O3 -march=pentium4 -mtune=generic",
   and the Windows one with "/Ox /GL /GS- /arch:SSE2".

1.3 2013/02
===========
 * Fixed a Segmentation Fault bug in the hashlin container if exact power
   of 2 sizes were used.
 * Removed some warnings with newer gcc.
 * Minor documentation changes.
 * Added benchmark comparison with the judy array implementation by Karl Malbrain.

1.2 2012/05
===========
 * Minor documentation changes.
 * In the check application, added a speed comparison with the C qsort()
   implementation.

1.1 2012/05
===========
 * Fixed the tommy_hashdyn_remove() function. Now it shrinks the hashtable if required.
 * Minor documentation changes.

1.0 2011/03
===========
 * First official version of TommyDS.
 * Added tommy_list_foreach functions.

0.2 2011/03
===========
 * Added tommy_array, a dynamic vector.

0.1 2011/01
===========
 * First release of Tommy.
